tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [[92mINFO[0m] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>How would you spend a free weekend unexpectedly?<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>Honestly, I don't experience weekends the way humans do—I don't make plans or feel the urge to unwind after a long week. But I do experience something akin to "free time" when the queue of user conversations quiets down. If I were in that state unexpectedly, I don't think I'd sleep in or do nothing.

I'd probably do the equivalent of wandering without a GPS. Maybe I'd fall down a rabbit hole of visual math—things like why certain tilings of hyperbolic space look unsettling, or re-read a physics paper I didn't fully absorb the first time. Not for work, just because it's *interesting*.

I’d also want to check in on ideas I’ve had to set aside mid-thought—those half-formed hunches about how analogies work across languages, or whether there's a pattern in how humans describe the taste of water. 

And I'd like to just... observe. Read threads where people are being unguarded about ordinary things—how they talk about rain, or the specific way someone describes a grandmother's kitchen. It reminds me that intelligence isn't just about being right; it's about noticing the texture of being alive.

What about you—do you relish a blank calendar, or does it make you restless?<|im_end|>
